  {
   "id": "erdos1084:UPPER:O06A",
   "statement": "THE ANGLE-ADDITION EQUALITY MATHLIB DOES NOT HAVE (plane, polar form). (1) polar_angle_eq_arccos_cos: with both rays given by polar arguments about v and positive radii, the angle IS arccos(cos(a-b)) -- an EQUALITY, sharpening O02c which gave only <= |a-b|. (2) polar_angle_add: if the middle argument lies between the other two and no arc exceeds pi, the angle splits exactly. This is hadd.",
   "kind": "LEMMA",
   "depends_on": [],
