   "backend": "box 51.158.234.15, lake env lean, Mathlib 919544d4, toolchain v4.31.0-rc1",
   "supersedes": null,
   "is_not_a_close_of": "erdos1084:UPPER:O06",
   "library_gap_closed": null,
   "retraction": "The ascending gap hypotheses and InsideAngleAt encode OPPOSITE orientations, so on the intended class of convex hull listings the hypotheses of o06_angle_sum_of_polar_fan are mutually unsatisfiable: the theorem is true and vacuous there. Measured on the unit square about the origin - counterclockwise (ascending) gives InsideAngleAt false at all four vertices, clockwise (descending) true at all four. It was offered to the producing lane UNMODELLED, which is why it survived. Superseded by erdos1084:UPPER:O06D, which is instantiated."
  },
  {
   "id": "erdos1084:UPPER:O06D",
   "statement": "THE ORIENTATION-CORRECT HANDOFF. Same as O06H but with DESCENDING central arguments (0 <= a i - a (i+1) <= pi, gap sum 2*pi), which is the orientation InsideAngleAt actually selects. hcentral_of_polar_desc survives unchanged because the central angle is arccos(cos d) and cosine is even. INSTANTIATED: o06_polar_fan_desc_model puts the clockwise square through the whole chain, so all four hypothesis families hold together - which the ascending version could not do.",
   "kind": "LEMMA",
   "depends_on": [
    "erdos1084:UPPER:O06I",
    "erdos1084:UPPER:O02C"
   ],
   "binding": "PARAPHRASE",
   "binding_detail": "a typed Lean obligation of the upper-bound ladder, stated over the target's own verbatim definitions",
   "status": "PROVED_KERNEL",
   "obligation": "interior angles of a convex h-gon sum to (h-2)*pi.",
